$$x - 2y = -7$$', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$4$"},{"key":"B","text":"$5$"},{"key":"C","text":"$7$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{23}{3}$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'A', NULL, E'Adding the two equations eliminates $y$: $(3x + 2y) + (x - 2y) = 23 + (-7)$, giving $4x = 16$, so $x = 4$. Computing $4x = 16$ but dividing as $16 \\div 4 = 5$ is an arithmetic slip. The value $7$ comes from computing $23 - 16 = 7$ without dividing by $2$, which is the intermediate step when solving for $y$ (misread question, solving for the wrong variable and stopping early). Dividing $23$ by $3$ treats the first equation as if $y = 0$ and solves only $3x = 23$ (partial reasoning, ignoring the system entirely).', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"arithmetic_slip"},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"misread_question"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"partial_reasoning"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 60, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-19"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-19","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);












































